textDisplay = NodePath("RichTextLabel")
textNotes = Dictionary[int, String]({
0: "I still remember this tragic day when a thunderstorm took away my home… It was raining still and the look on my peers… We all were scared, even the children. That day everyone lost something. As the head of the village… I had to take them somewhere safe… I didn’t want to put them at risk in these conditions…",
1: "Even though I was little, I clearly  remember his exact expression. At that time he was the head of the village and as I grow older and older I think I understand his pain for his decision. We had only a few cows left for around 40 - 50 people and not a lot of flour. That year we had a weak produce, the sun did not spare us.",
2: "I still get goosebumps when I think about that day, the thunderstorm destroyed everything… I was a scared young girl, I was going to marry my first love… I still miss him sometimes… And the sad thing is that we had to bury him in a hurry… Winter was coming and we had to move fast or else…",
3: "I am glad that I have a place to call home, thanks to this cave we managed to survive thanks to the gems and the drinkable lake water inside it. Also now we are closer to the other villages as well. Even though we lost a lot, now thanks to the Goddess Iacinthina we now have an easier life. I am glad that we live with my peers near her.",
4: "Oohh… I remember when Goddess Iacinthina appeared in my dream and chose me as her Lux, to spread her word to the people and to warn them about the Exchange. We have to bring her goods from the outside world to her and sometimes we receive bigger and rarer gems. ",
5: "Haha, now I know how to write :D My brother won’t be happy with what I am about to write. ehh, he won’t find out, I will make sure to hide it well. So one day my brother got a little bit greedy and he took more gemstones that he needed. Ms. Goddess saw that and sent a small lighting string to his buttocks ;D Still funny I can’t stop laughing. I hope this note leaves a mark in the future.",
6: "Thanks to these jewels, of the most mesmerizing kind, I managed with my limited tools to make a beautiful “be my forever” ring. She loved it and wore it for almost 30 years. We still visit Goddess Iacinthina from time to time to give her some flowers, bread, silk and jewelry. We share our lives with her, I think she is happy for us."
})
